-- NEWER VGM SEGA/Atlus — Section 11 (Super Monkey Ball)
--
-- Source: reference/NEWER VGM Sound Sources - SEGAAtlus.csv lines 1860-2175.
-- 10 game records, ~296 usage rows.
--
-- The Super Monkey Ball franchise spans 2001 (Arcade Monkey Ball) through
-- 2019 (Banana Blitz HD). SMB 3D is the largest single-game entry by far
-- (~109 rows including 14 unused-track rows from the Vendor Pop unused
-- music). Heavy sample-CD reliance throughout, especially Norman Cook's
-- "Skip to my Loops" (resurfaces in SMB 3D and Step & Roll).
--
-- Verbatim preservations (Rule 2):
--   - "Mellotron Archives" (T2040) is created as a NEW manufacturer here
--     for SMB Step & Roll's "Michael Pinder Presents Mellotron" library.
--     This is contributor inconsistency with the existing
--     "Mike Pinder / Mellotron Archives" product from JSRF — same library
--     family, different attribution. Both preserved.
--   - "Freeze Records / Trey Max Top Secret CD Beats Vol. 3" (T2091)
--     preserved distinct from existing "Trey Max - Top Secret CD Beats
--     Vol. 3" (with hyphen). Punctuation difference, same library.
--   - "Roland / SR-JV80-10 Bass & Drum" (T1931) preserved distinct from
--     existing "Roland / SR-JV80-10" (no descriptor). Same expansion
--     board, different verbatim names.
--   - "Sample: Gorillaz - 2023-04-05 00:00:00" (SMB 3D T2048) — the CSV
--     value appears to be Excel mangling of the original song title
--     (likely "5/4" parsed as a date and reformatted). Preserved literally;
--     not retroactively corrected per Rule 2.
--   - "Monster Pack Sound Library 12,000 " (T2082-2087) — product name
--     has embedded comma and trailing space; preserved verbatim.
--   - "The Nightingale ""Voice Box""" (T2147-2148) — product name with
--     literal quotes around "Voice Box" preserved.
--   - "Features a sample taken from Stump - Charlton Heston " note
--     trailing space preserved (T2065).
--   - Multiple "Roland,JV-2080 " trailing-space variants throughout
--     SMB/SMB2 merge via NOCASE with existing JV-2080 product.
--   - SMB 3D "Unused Tracks" sub-section (T2141-2155) ingested as
--     category='unused' for the "VENDOR POP" placeholder song.

